        "original_id": "444b256e-aa44-51e6-8fb9-8c96c5782c5a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Myles Kennedy, Mark Tremonti, Michael \"Elvis\" Baskette\n- Bands: Alter Bridge, Myles Kennedy and the Conspirators, SafetySuit\n- Places: Tulsa, Oklahoma, Nashville, Tennessee\n- Songs: \"Rise Today\"\n- Albums: Blackbird, Life Left to Go\n- Record Labels: Universal Motown Records\n\nFacts:\n- Myles Kennedy, born Myles Richard Bass on November 27, 1969, is an American musician, singer, and songwriter.\n- Myles Kennedy is the lead vocalist and rhythm guitarist of Alter Bridge.\n- Myles Kennedy is also the lead vocalist in Slash's backing band, Myles Kennedy and the Conspirators.\n- \"Rise Today\" was written by Alter Bridge lead guitarist Mark Tremonti and lead vocalist Myles Kennedy.\n- \"Rise Today\" was produced by Michael \"Elvis\" Baskette and featured on Alter Bridge's 2007 second studio album Blackbird.\n- SafetySuit is an American pop rock and alternative rock band from Tulsa, Oklahoma, that is currently based in Nashville, Tennessee.\n- SafetySuit released its debut studio album, Life Left to Go, on May 13, 2008, through Universal Motown Records.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
